  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The equations of two waves are given by :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>These waves are simultaneously passing through a string. The amplitude of the resulting wave is :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
